sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (docs/reference/development-containers.md#complete-a-clone and #a-clone-create-is-two-operations): the second Operation of a clone create. It starts the Processes, fills the database, starts a nested fleet, publishes the Route when its create did not, and checks the clone; only its success makes the clone `active`.
  %% Decided by the owner (2026-11-14): the create publishes the address when its Route Nodes are free at admission (container/create.mmd). The completion publishes only a Route that is not published: Nodes held at the create's admission, a publication that failed in the create, or a retry after a failed publication.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:complete
  %% kind: instance.complete
  autonumber
  %% lane CL icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CL as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>Instance container
  CL->>GW: instance:complete INSTANCE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:complete 42`
  %%> - syntax: `instance:complete <instance> [--json]`
  %%> Callers:
  %%> - the command, to retry after a failed completion
  %%> - the create's terminal projection, in the same transaction that ends the create
  Note over GW: Check the clone<br/>take the Instance lock
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - a container clone, `source_resolved`, with its starting commit recorded
  %%> - its T3 server is registered
  %%> - no other Operation holds the Instance
  %%> Captures:
  %%> - the create's admitted database plan and Processes
  %%> - a Route whose sites are not published: its publication from the current site catalog, and its serving Nodes held from admission to the end, as Route create does
  %%> - a Route the create published: no publication and no Node hold
  alt a check fails
    %% path: refused
    GW--xCL: Refused<br/>instance.complete_unavailable
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing changes; no Operation starts
    %%> - a held Instance lock refuses with `operation.target_busy`
  else nothing is left on the Node
    %% path: engine
    Note over GW: End at once on the engine<br/>clone active, no Swamp run
    %%> When: the create said `services: seed` (the seed holds the services part), and there is no database, Valkey user, Route publication or fleet start
    %%> The engine runs it with no step; its projection makes the clone `active` as a succeeded run does
  else the clone can be completed
    %% path: main
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-complete
    %%> What it sends:
    %%> - the intent with the launcher program, and one vault copy: the release scripts beside the Process files, one line
    GW-->>CL: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation ID
    opt a database
      SW->>N: Create the database<br/>database steps · SSH
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - the clone's own database on the default's server, then a copy of the default's data; the clone's own Valkey user beside it
      %%> On failure:
      %%> - `failed_step: database`
    end
    opt a nested-fleet clone whose fleet does not start in the background
      SW->>N: Start the fleet<br/>clone-fleet · Ansible
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - runs only when the create's result has no `fleet_start: background`: a Swamp create, or a seed without the tunnel's boot unit
      %%> - starts the nested containers and waits for Doctor and the three agents
      %%> - runs under `ic-clone-fleet-<node>-<instance id % 64>`, one of 64 names per Node; copies started at once start their fleets side by side, because Swamp fails a step that waits 60 s for a name another run holds
      %%> On failure:
      %%> - `failed_step: fleet` with the fleet phase's code
    end
    SW->>N: Start, check services<br/>clone-services · SSH
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - one dispatch: stages the release scripts from the completion's one copy into this run's own private folder; the create's folder is not read
    %%> - the services: PHP settings, file rights, Process files, web config, the Node store, then the units
    %%> - file rights: root's workspace pass, the same program as a deployment's (swamp/ansible/instance_workspace_owner.py): the group gets back what the owner has, and `agent` gets each entry that `orbit` owns, a link itself and never its target (ADR 0268); a copy of an older seed gets its owner here
    %%> - refuses when the checkout mark names another Instance
    %%> - writes no tracked file: the user's work in the checkout stays as it is
    %%> - then the check: the checkout mark, the agent's Git identity, PHP and every running unit
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the stage or the services: `failed_step: workspace`
    %%> - a dead unit: `failed_step: check`, `instance.container_process_inactive` with its `process_failure` receipt
    opt a Route its create did not publish
      SW->>N: Publish the Route<br/>operation-route-create
      %%> When:
      %%> - in its own job, beside the container steps from the run's start
      %%> - only when the admission captured the Route: Nodes held at the create's admission, `route_publication: failed`, or a retry after a failed publication
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - the Route create children unchanged: CSR, sign, site, TLS probe
      %%> On failure:
      %%> - `failed_step: route`
    end
    alt the run succeeds
      %% path: completed
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
      Note over GW: Record active<br/>one transaction
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the Route is `active`, then the Instance `active` with `first_setup_pending` false
      %%> - for a task copy, in the same transaction, its reserved task runs and the task's completion-failure assistance request ends; any other request stays
    else a step fails or the run is cancelled
      %% path: failed
      SW->>N: Withdraw the Route<br/>route-withdraw
      %%> When:
      %%> - only when this run's Route step ran; no half Route stays
      %%> - an address the create published stays up, answering 502, until a retry or `instance:destroy`, which withdraws it; a retry that succeeds keeps it as it is
      SW--xGW: Run failed or cancelled<br/>failed step, error_code
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the Instance stays `source_resolved` with `failed_step` and `error_code`; the container keeps running and T3 keeps its thread
      %%> - `recovery.retry.command` is `instance:complete`; `instance:destroy` removes the clone
      %%> - for a task copy, Orbit keeps the copy: its task stays `reserved` and asks for assistance with this retry
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - the same command runs the whole completion again, with the steps a create retry runs
    end
  end
  loop until terminal
    CL->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CL: Status and result
  end
